Applied on top of https://github.com/andrewleech/qwen3-asr-onnx (main, 2026-09-02) before
running `export.py`. The upstream prefill graph emits logits for every prompt position
([1, T, 151936] fp32 — ~120 MB for a 200-token prompt), which on WebGPU is a per-utterance
GPU→CPU readback that would dominate the prefill time. Greedy decoding only needs the last
position, so slice before lm_head.

--- a/src/decoder_wrapper.py
+++ b/src/decoder_wrapper.py
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ class DecoderInitWrapper(nn.Module):
             all_values.append(value_states)

         hidden_states = self.norm(hidden_states)
-        logits = self.lm_head(hidden_states)
+        logits = self.lm_head(hidden_states[:, -1:, :])  # spike: last position only

         present_keys = torch.stack(all_keys, dim=0)
         present_values = torch.stack(all_values, dim=0)
